# Two cores, one board
# Level 5 - Advanced
#
# An ESP32 counts on its second core and reports to the main one through a queue - no races.
# You learn: 'on core 1' runs a task on the second core, Queue passes values between cores safely.
# You need: a dual-core ESP32 board (board.cores is 2 or more) and an LED on GPIO25.

board esp32
use mujard.queue

led = pin GPIO25 as output

q = Queue(int, 8)                  # up to 8 ints waiting between the cores

task counter on core 1:            # this task runs on the second core
    while true:
        for n in 1..=10:
            q.push(n)
            wait 200 ms            # wait is allowed inside a task
        q.push(0)                  # 0 = "one round done"

every 100 ms:                      # the main core drains the queue
    while q.available:
        print "core 1 says {q.pop()}"

every 1 s:                         # and keeps its own life going
    led.toggle()
    print "main core busy too ({board.cores} cores in use)"
